    id: "intro",
    title: "Introducing yourself",
    blurb: "Give your name, say where you are from and where you live, give your age, and ask the same back.",
    deck: "About me",
    body: `
<p>Meeting people in Cebu, you will be asked the same few things: your name, where you are from, and often your age. This lesson gives you all of them, in the order people usually ask. Questions about age are common and not meant to be rude, so it helps to have the answer ready.</p>
<h3>My name is…</h3>
<p>English says "I'm Emma". Cebuano says <b>Ako si Emma</b>: the full form <b>ako</b>, then the name with its marker <b>si</b>. The short <b>ko</b> cannot start a sentence, so here it has to be <b>ako</b>.</p>
{{ex:Ako si Emma.|ah-KOH see ehm-mah|I'm Emma.}}
<p>To ask a name: <b>Unsa ang imong ngalan?</b>, "What is your name?" In speech, <b>unsa ang</b> shrinks to <b>unsay</b>. <b>imong</b> means "your"; like <b>akong</b>, it goes before the noun and ends in -ng.</p>
{{ex:Unsay imong ngalan?|oon-sai ee-mohng NGAH-lahn|What's your name?}}
<h3>Where are you from?</h3>
<p><b>Taga-</b> means "from", and it joins the place with a hyphen: <b>Taga-Amerika ko</b>, "I'm from the US". To ask, join it to <b>asa</b> (where). The place comes first and the short pronoun second.</p>
{{ex:Taga-Amerika ko.|tah-gah-ah-meh-ree-kah koh|I'm from the US.}}
{{ex:Taga-asa ka?|tah-gah-ah-sah kah|Where are you from?}}
<p>Do not translate "Where are you from?" word for word: <b>Asa ka gikan?</b> means "Where have you just been?"</p>
<h3>Where I live</h3>
<p>Learn this sentence whole for now; its verb comes in a later lesson: <b>Nagpuyo ko sa Cebu</b>, "I live in Cebu". Swap in your own town after <b>sa</b>.</p>
{{ex:Nagpuyo ko sa Cebu.|nahg-poo-yoh koh sah seh-BOO|I live in Cebu.}}
<h3>Age</h3>
<p>English "is" thirty; some languages "have" thirty years. Cebuano gives the age in Spanish numbers with <b>anyos</b> (years), main word first: <b>Traynta anyos ko</b>. The numbers come later; for now, learn this one pattern.</p>
{{ex:Traynta anyos ko.|train-tah ahn-yohs koh|I'm thirty.}}
<h3>Nice to meet you</h3>
<p>Also learned whole: <b>Nalipay ko nga nakaila nimo</b>, "I'm glad to have met you". A smile and <b>Salamat</b> work too.</p>
{{ex:Nalipay ko nga nakaila nimo.|nah-lee-pai koh ngah nah-kah-ee-lah nee-moh|Nice to meet you.}}
<div class="tip"><b>Most common mistake:</b> copying English "Where are you from?". <b>Asa ka gikan?</b> → <b>Taga-asa ka?</b></div>
`,
